From: ArchivalEra <archivalera@localhost>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/gic: hi3798mv310: keep Group 1 enabled and dump
 banked SGI/PPI state

The hi3798mv310 board (poplar-derived hi3798mv2x TF-A, GIC-400,
Cortex-A53 x4) deadlocks in SMP bringup because no GIC interrupt is
ever delivered to any CPU.

Runtime non-secure reads of the fully-initialized kernel show a GIC
that looks correctly enabled (GICD_CTLR=0x1 in the NS view, IGROUPR0
with SGIs and timer PPIs in Group 1, GICC_CTLR=0x3e3), so the two
"findings" that motivated the previous fix attempts are retracted:

 1. "ISENABLER0 == 0 (SGIs never enabled)" was read from 0xf1001104,
    which is GICD_ISENABLER1 (SPI 32-63).  That register reads 0 after
    gic_dist_config() disables all SPIs - that is normal.  The real
    GICD_ISENABLER0 is at dist+0x100 = 0xf1001100 and is written with
    0xffff (GICD_INT_EN_SET_SGI) by gic_cpu_config() on every CPU.

 2. "GICD_CTLR == 0x1 means the kernel cleared EnableGrp1" is a
    banked-view misread: in the non-secure view of GICD_CTLR, bit 0 is
    the alias of EnableGrp1(NS), so 0x1 is the *good* state.

Since the reference board (hi3798mv300) runs four cores, arch timer
PPIs and SGIs with the same TF-A platform and an unmodified mainline
kernel, none of the Group/enable theory explains the failure by
itself.  This patch therefore:

 - keeps the already-validated harmless belt-and-braces writes
   (GICC_CTLR.EnableGrp1, GICD_CTLR bit 1, IGROUPR0 = all Group 1), and

 - adds a one-shot per-CPU dump of the banked SGI/PPI state with the
   register offsets spelled out in the message itself, so the next
   serial log cannot be misread the same way.

The decisive next experiments (software-pended PPI/SGI bisection from
the initramfs) are documented in docs/mv310-gic-bisect-runbook.md.
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-gic.c | 53 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 52 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic.c
@@ -457,7 +457,15 @@
 	bypass = readl(cpu_base + GIC_CPU_CTRL);
 	bypass &= GICC_DIS_BYPASS_MASK;
 
-	writel_relaxed(bypass | mode | GICC_ENABLE, cpu_base + GIC_CPU_CTRL);
+	/*
+	 * hi3798mv310: also set GICC_CTLR.EnableGrp1 (bit 1). The
+	 * poplar-derived BL31 only programs the secure view of the CPU
+	 * interface; in some banked configurations bit 1 is what gates
+	 * Group 1 delivery. For a plain non-secure GIC-400 view bit 0 is
+	 * already the EnableGrp1(NS) alias, so this is harmless.
+	 */
+	writel_relaxed(bypass | mode | GICC_ENABLE |
+		       GIC_CPU_CTRL_EnableGrp1, cpu_base + GIC_CPU_CTRL);
 }
 
 
@@ -481,7 +489,23 @@
 
 	gic_dist_config(base, gic_irqs, GICD_INT_DEF_PRI);
 
-	writel_relaxed(GICD_ENABLE, base + GIC_DIST_CTRL);
+	/*
+	 * hi3798mv310: force SGI/PPI (INTID 0-31) into Group 1 in the
+	 * non-secure banked view. The poplar-derived BL31 only programs
+	 * the secure bank through gicv2_secure_ppi_sgi_setup_props();
+	 * whether the NS alias needs this write varies, but it is
+	 * harmless on GIC-400.
+	 */
+	writel_relaxed(0xffffffff, base + GIC_DIST_IGROUP);
+
+	/*
+	 * GICD_ENABLE is bit 0; in the non-secure view that bit is the
+	 * alias of EnableGrp1(NS). Also set GICD_CTLR.EnableGrp1 (bit 1,
+	 * same encoding as the GICC field) so the distributor forwards
+	 * Group 1 under either banking interpretation.
+	 */
+	writel_relaxed(GICD_ENABLE | GIC_CPU_CTRL_EnableGrp1,
+		       base + GIC_DIST_CTRL);
 }
 
 static int gic_cpu_init(struct gic_chip_data *gic)
@@ -521,6 +545,25 @@
 	writel_relaxed(GICC_INT_PRI_THRESHOLD, base + GIC_CPU_PRIMASK);
 	gic_cpu_if_up(gic);
 
+	/*
+	 * hi3798mv310 bring-up aid: dump the banked SGI/PPI state exactly
+	 * as this CPU's non-secure view sees it, with offsets spelled out
+	 * so a serial log cannot be misread again.  Note the trap that
+	 * cost a full investigation day: GICD_ISENABLER0 is at dist+0x100
+	 * (0xf1001100); 0xf1001104 is GICD_ISENABLER1 (SPI 32-63) and
+	 * reads 0 after gic_dist_config() disables all SPIs, which is
+	 * normal and does NOT mean the SGIs are disabled.
+	 */
+	pr_info("MV310-GIC[%u]: GICD_CTLR(+0x000)=0x%08x GICD_TYPER(+0x004)=0x%08x IGROUPR0(+0x080)=0x%08x ISENABLER0(+0x100)=0x%08x ICFGR1(+0xc04)=0x%08x GICC_CTLR(+0x000)=0x%08x GICC_PMR(+0x004)=0x%08x\n",
+		cpu,
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + GIC_DIST_CTRL),
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + 0x004),
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + GIC_DIST_IGROUP),
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + GIC_DIST_ENABLE_SET),
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + GIC_DIST_CONFIG + 0x4),
+		readl_relaxed(base + GIC_CPU_CTRL),
+		readl_relaxed(base + GIC_CPU_PRIMASK));
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
